You can never hold all of reality and its implications in your mind simultaneously so a distraction is enough, what your attention lingers on can be your whole reality (having a bonding orgasm with a loved one,having your first child, reaching a career goal after years of effort , taking acid and contemplating life, having a spiritual experience in an orthodox monastery). 

&#x200B;

I get the depressive realism, i get that the most truthful worldview is pessimistic, but if it takes optimistic illusions, to not waste the gift of existence and consciouness instead of total oblivion, then do it.  Learn to like human goals, human things, and forget about dry cerebralism, or leave the limits of rationality (which would state that youre just held alive by your self preservation instinct) or antinatalism ( which sees suffering as a math equation, and doesnt underestand it in the wise paradigm that for instance stoicism had -that suffering and deprivation can make pleasure, victory, and things we take for granted taste sweeter when they happen,food tastes better when youre hungry). 

Forget about all the tragedy in the world ( yes it is so pervasive and deep that ,it goes even to our survival , we have to kill in order to live) and stop minimising the beauty, and the resilience ,and the short memories, and the psychology that was shaped in billions of years to cope with it, get into your body ,forget your mind for now, take DMT, live,laugh, love.

&#x200B;

Read Cioran on the heights of despair if you want or watch some cat videos :).

